            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention discloses a parameter upgrade system comprising: a physiological monitor having a sensor port configured to attach and communicate with a sensor; a processor board in communications with the sensor port having a board digital signal processor (DSP); a plurality of firmware instructions residing on the processor board and executable by the board DSP so as to calculate a plurality of physiological parameters in response to a sensor signal received from the sensor and determine an enable state for each of the plurality of physiological parameters; and a plurality of handheld upgrade tools individually attachable to the sensor port in lieu of the sensor, wherein each of the plurality of handheld upgrade tools comprises: a tool digital signal processor (DSP) configured to provide changes to the plurality of firmware instructions and configured to, update, based on a verification that a parameter upgrade is available, an enable state of a physiological parameter to make the physiological parameter available for output by the monitor, wherein making the physiological parameter available for output by the monitor enables the sensor port to calculate at least one additional physiological parameter in response to the sensor; a sensor port connector that mates directly with the sensor port and provides a communications path between the tool DSP and the board DSP; an I/O port connector that provides communications between the tool DSP and an external digital device; and an information element that identifies the handheld upgrade tool to the board DSP.</p>
